.TH "SERIALPORT" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort \- SerialPort
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] interface of the Web Serial API provides
access to a serial port on the host device.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
Instances of this interface may be obtained by calling methods of the
\f[CR]Serial\f[R] interface, therefore it has no constructor of its own.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.connected\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a boolean value that indicates whether the port is logically
connected to the device.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.readable\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] for receiving data from the device
connected to the port.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.writable\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]WritableStream\f[R] for sending data to the device
connected to the port.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.forget()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when access to the serial
port is revoked.
Calling this \(lqforgets\(rq the device, resetting any previously\-set
permissions so the calling site can no longer communicate with the port.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.getInfo()\f[R]
Returns an object containing identifying information for the device
available via the port.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.open()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when the port is opened.
By default the port is opened with 8 data bits, 1 stop bit and no parity
checking.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.setSignals()\f[R]
Sets control signals on the port and returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that
resolves when they are set.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.getSignals()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an object containing the
current state of the port\(cqs control signals.
.TP
\f[B]SerialPort.close()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves when the port closes.
.SH EVENTS
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R]
Fired when the port connects to the device.
.TP
\f[B]disconnect\f[R]
Fired when the port disconnects from the device.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Opening a port
Before communicating on a serial port it must be opened.
Opening the port allows the site to specify the necessary parameters
that control how data is transmitted and received.
Developers should check the documentation for the device they are
connecting to for the appropriate parameters.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]await\f[R] port.open({ baudRate: 9600 \f[I]/* pick your baud rate */\f[R] });
.EE
.PP
Once the \f[CR]Promise\f[R] returned by \f[CR]open()\f[R] resolves the
\f[CR]readable\f[R] and \f[CR]writable\f[R] attributes can be accessed
to get the \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] and \f[CR]WritableStream\f[R]
instances for receiving data from and sending data to the connected
device.
.SS Reading data from a port
The following example shows how to read data from a port.
The outer loop handles non\-fatal errors, creating a new reader until a
fatal error is encountered and \f[CR]readable\f[R] becomes
\f[CR]null\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]while\f[R] (port.readable) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] reader = port.readable.getReader();
  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[B]while\f[R] (\f[B]true\f[R]) {
      \f[B]const\f[R] { value, done } = \f[B]await\f[R] reader.read();
      \f[B]if\f[R] (done) {
        \f[I]// |reader| has been canceled.\f[R]
        \f[B]break\f[R];
      }
      \f[I]// Do something with |value|\&...\f[R]
    }
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] (error) {
    \f[I]// Handle |error|\&...\f[R]
  } \f[B]finally\f[R] {
    reader.releaseLock();
  }
}
.EE
.SS Writing data to a port
The following example shows how to write a string to a port.
A \f[CR]TextEncoder\f[R] converts the string to a \f[CR]Uint8Array\f[R]
before transmission.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] encoder = \f[B]new\f[R] TextEncoder();
\f[B]const\f[R] writer = port.writable.getWriter();
\f[B]await\f[R] writer.write(encoder.encode(\(dqPING\(dq));
writer.releaseLock();
.EE
